From: Claude (Anthropic AI) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Drop the duplicate PE-side event reader thread.

The wineland-child-rendering series moves Wayland event dispatching to a
unix-side thread: waylanddrv_unix_init() now spawns wayland_event_dispatcher()
via PsCreateSystemThread(), which calls waylanddrv_unix_read_events().

An earlier patch in the stack is supposed to remove the old PE-side
wayland_read_events_thread() from DllMain, but on the current wine pin GNU
patch misdetects those two hunks as "Reversed (or previously applied)" and
silently skips them. The old thread therefore survives and DllMain still
creates it, so two threads end up calling waylanddrv_unix_read_events()
concurrently on the same process-global Wayland connection.

Remove the PE-side thread explicitly so only the unix-side dispatcher reads
events. This performs exactly what the skipped hunks intended.

Note this only reproduces when building proton-ge-custom master (currently
22 commits past GE-Proton11-6) against wine 9358696fe9a.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/dllmain.c | 16 ----------------
 1 file changed, 16 deletions(-)

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/dllmain.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/dllmain.c
@@ -27,20 +27,6 @@
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(waylanddrv);
 
-static DWORD WINAPI wayland_read_events_thread(void *arg)
-{
-    const THREAD_NAME_INFORMATION info = {RTL_CONSTANT_STRING(L"winewayland_dispatcher")};
-    NtSetInformationThread(GetCurrentThread(), ThreadNameInformation, &info, sizeof(info));
-
-    WAYLANDDRV_UNIX_CALL(read_events, NULL);
-    /* This thread terminates only if an unrecoverable error occurred
-     * during event reading (e.g., the connection to the Wayland
-     * compositor is broken). */
-    ERR("Failed to read events from the compositor, terminating process\n");
-    TerminateProcess(GetCurrentProcess(), 1);
-    return 0;
-}
-
 static LRESULT CALLBACK clipboard_wndproc(HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wp, LPARAM lp)
 {
     switch (msg)
@@ -111,8 +97,6 @@
     if (WAYLANDDRV_UNIX_CALL(init, NULL))
         return FALSE;
 
-    /* Read wayland events from a dedicated thread. */
-    CloseHandle(CreateThread(NULL, 0, wayland_read_events_thread, NULL, 0, &tid));
     /* Handle clipboard events in a dedicated thread, if needed. */
     if (!WAYLANDDRV_UNIX_CALL(init_clipboard, NULL))
         CloseHandle(CreateThread(NULL, 0, clipboard_thread, NULL, 0, &tid));
